        "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}={b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=-{b}_{2}?$",
        "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-4{b}_{2}-7{b}_{3} \\\\  & =4{b}_{1}-7{b}_{3}-4{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4({b}_{1})-7({b}_{3})+4(-{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-7{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$",
